HUMAN: Round 1 analysed — 3 visual-quality upgrades: atmospheric sky, terrain macro detail, shadow presets.
FIND F1 sev=H tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:2911-2938#"const skyMat = new THREE.ShaderMaterial" what="sky is 2-stop gradient; no sun disc, no mie halo around sun, no horizon band, no stars at night — despite full TOD driver computing solarElev/daylight/twilight" fix="rewrite skyMat fragment: add uniforms sunDirection(vec3)/daylight(float)/twilight(float)/lowPoly(float); render soft sun disc + mie forward-scatter halo + horizon saturation band + hash21-based star field faded in by (1-daylight); drive new uniforms from TOD block (same site that writes topColor/bottomColor) and from biome apply site" ref=flight-sim3.html:9999-10001#"skyMat.uniforms.topColor.value.copy",flight-sim3.html:7397-7398#"skyMat.uniforms.topColor.value.setHex",flight-sim3.html:9945-9967 dep=-
FIND F2 sev=M tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:3015-3082#"void main" what="SAND_FS has ripple normals+sparkle but zero macro albedo variation — terrain reads flat single-color at 100-800m; only per-vertex colors break it up" fix="add 2-octave vnoise macro patchiness: low-freq (uv*0.004 and uv*0.018) value noise modulating vColor +/-8% luminance and warm/cool hue shift, gated by flatness so cliffs unaffected; reuse existing vnoise/hash21 — no new textures, ~6 ALU lines" ref=flight-sim3.html:2999-3013#"float hash21" dep=-
FIND F3 sev=M tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:2947-2956#"sun.shadow.mapSize.set(1024, 1024)" what="shadow map fixed 1024px + 230m box regardless of gfx preset; blocky aircraft/structure shadows on high-end machines" fix="gate by existing gfx preset system (P-key panel, localStorage gfx-settings-v1): high=2048, ultra=4096 mapSize, keep 230m box; apply on preset change requires sun.shadow.map.dispose()+null so map reallocates" ref=flight-sim3.html:2736#"renderer.setPixelRatio" dep=-
